==Trivia==
*Urs is the rider, Fenrir is the wolf.
*The name Urs (ウルス ''Urusu'') may be derived from ウルズ ''Uruzu'' ([[wikipedia:Urðr|Urðr]], one of the three goddesses of fate in Norse mythology), ''urus'' (Malay and Indonesian for "to manage"), ''uruş'' (Turkmen for war), or the feminine given name ''Ursula''. Where the other [[wikipedia:Verðandi|Verðandi]] and [[wikipedia:Skuld|Skuld]] represent the present and future, respectively, Urðr represents the past, correlating with Urs & Fenrir's [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relic]] trait; the three [[wikipedia:Norns|Norns]] live beneath and tend to the world tree, [[wikipedia:Yggdrasil|Yggdrasil]], which may be represented by the [[Media:Bg1028.gif|huge, glowing tree]] in the last four [[Uncanny Legends]] stages.
**It may also be derived from ''c<u>urs</u>e'', though this is less likely, as ''curse'' transliterated into Japanese is カース ''kāsu''.
*In Norse mythology, [[wikipedia:Fenrir|Fenrir]] is a monstrous wolf and child of Loki and a giantess, Angrboða.
*Urs is potentially an ancestor of [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun]], as referred to in the ending of [[Stories of Legend]].

